  a: open-vocabulary
  b: closed-vocabulary
split: genuinely-split
draft_status: axis-only
leverage: 14.4
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(12) x split_weight(1) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  On vocabulary closure — whether a term set is fixed and enumerable, or may
  grow freely as records need new words — the records assert both open
  vocabulary (5 judgments, 0 authored) and closed vocabulary (7 judgments, 3
  authored). Which should be the stated rule, and where is the exception?

why_it_matters: >
  Until this is answered, a record below Dave inherits whichever side it happens
  to copy. Full draft pending: the proposal batch for this axis did not
  complete; the axis, poles, counts and evidence are real, the options below are
  the generic form.

